{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>For, etc.</b> The sense: that You are our Father and we are Your children, and You are a Father who shall be found forever." "And he mentioned Abraham, for he was the first who cut a covenant with HaShem, to be for him as Elohim and for his children, and he mentioned also Jacob, for he is the last of the patriarchs, and he is our root alone." "<b>will acknowledge us.</b> Like הבדל — He will separate us (Isaiah 56:4)."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 63, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:00:50.430561207Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}